{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447852-objects-of-madness-or-enlightenment","id":1447852,"title":"Objects of Madness... or Enlightenment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-07T15:24:20-07:00","id":1447852,"title":"Objects of Madness... or Enlightenment","content":"The idea here is to create an object whose dimensions are so complex that another Mage using sensory Magick to examine it is put at risk of their mind being overloaded. The three most important spheres, I believe, would be Matter, Correspondence and Entropy, in that order. Prime 2, if it was not previously something else turned into this object. <br /> <br /> It isn't specifically a Mind effect, since it is the complexity and, perhaps, connection to the rest of the universe that overwhelms the observer. <br /> <br /> It could also be a teaching tool that tests the worthiness of a Mage to learn higher Sphere levels.<br /> <br /> What Spheres and ranks are needed?<br /> What other applications could such an object have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T02:22:08-07:00","id":1448036,"title":"","content":"Were I to design some kind of Mobius-tesseract Calabi-Yau manifold type shape, I'd not create an object but rather enchant something, like a kaleidoscope or Viewmaster, such that peering into it would entrap the mind. So Correspondence, Mind, and Prime would be the spheres of choice, with creation requiring serious mathematical knowledge or, if going for something more mystically labyrinthine, Enigmas. <br /> <br /> If a device that connects the mage to the universe in some manner is what you're looking for, an elaborate orrery might work (think a more advanced model than that in the <i>Dark Crystal</i>). Matter is only necessary if its motions won't follow the natural geometry of its design. But it sounds like you want a puzzle machine, so Matter 4 (and Entropy 1 or 2 if you want those motions to be truly random). I'm not sure Correspondence is necessary; the &quot;mind overloaded&quot; aspect of the device seems to make it a Mind effect. <br /> <br /> For other applications...if you could arcanely link it to some other complex system, like a business or social group or spread of disease, you might scry with it, gaining an understanding (with Time) of its trends. It would be an excellent meditative device for a Seeking as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T23:22:53-07:00","id":1448202,"title":"","content":"I agree that the mind-overloading effect would need to involve the Mind sphere, whatever the specific rationale for how it works in-game. Well, I guess Entropy 5 could also serve the same purpose if one is a master of that sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T16:28:36-07:00","id":1448267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447852-objects-of-madness-or-enlightenment?p=1448036#post1448036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were I to design some kind of Mobius-tesseract Calabi-Yau manifold type shape, I'd not create an object but rather enchant something, like a kaleidoscope or Viewmaster, such that peering into it would entrap the mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few weeks ago, I made a mobius strip out of paper and scotch tape to show someone. She was sure that when she cut it in half, there would be two pieces. It was like like awakening a Sleeper. A Viewmaster gives you more control over who is allowed to see the thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447852-objects-of-madness-or-enlightenment?p=1448036#post1448036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Correspondence, Mind, and Prime would be the spheres of choice, with creation requiring serious mathematical knowledge or, if going for something more mystically labyrinthine, Enigmas.<br /> <br /> If a device that connects the mage to the universe in some manner is what you're looking for, an elaborate orrery might work (think a more advanced model than that in the <i>Dark Crystal</i>). Matter is only necessary if its motions won't follow the natural geometry of its design. But it sounds like you want a puzzle machine, so Matter 4 (and Entropy 1 or 2 if you want those motions to be truly random). I'm not sure Correspondence is necessary; the &quot;mind overloaded&quot; aspect of the device seems to make it a Mind effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking Correspondence at its highest rank, Spatial Mutation and Co-Location, in combination with Matter 4. Take an object that is sitting still, laid over a floor. Take the space that one edge occupies and spatially blend that space with the space another edge occupies, using Matter to fuse the edges together. The center remains untouched. Then, add Entropy to cause the most complex interplay of material-spatial connections to occur. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447852-objects-of-madness-or-enlightenment?p=1448202#post1448202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the mind-overloading effect would need to involve the Mind sphere, whatever the specific rationale for how it works in-game. Well, I guess Entropy 5 could also serve the same purpose if one is a master of that sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vote carried. Mind 4, Alter Consciousness. This forces the viewer's mind to process the full complexity of the object until it is understood or their psyche shuts down.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447852-objects-of-madness-or-enlightenment?p=1448036#post1448036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For other applications...if you could arcanely link it to some other complex system, like a business or social group or spread of disease, you might scry with it, gaining an understanding (with Time) of its trends. It would be an excellent meditative device for a Seeking as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking of making such an object the center of the plot for the next chapter in my Mage Chronicle. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}